=== TITLE: B-Scan Ultrasonography of Eyes (Bilateral Ocular USG) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL BILATERAL OCULAR B-SCAN ULTRASOUND STUDY.
- Clear vitreous cavities bilaterally with intact retinal attachments.
- No evidence of retinal detachment, vitreous hemorrhage, or intraocular mass lesion.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: B-SCAN ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF BOTH EYES (OCULAR USG)

OBSERVATIONS:
- ANTERIOR SEGMENTS: Bilateral anterior chambers, corneas, and crystalline lenses are in normal anatomical position and configuration.
- VITREOUS CAVITIES:
  * Right Eye (OD): Vitreous cavity is clear and acoustically anechoic. No mobile vitreous opacities, membranes, or vitreous hemorrhage.
  * Left Eye (OS): Vitreous cavity is clear and acoustically anechoic. No mobile vitreous opacities, membranes, or vitreous hemorrhage.
- CHORIO-RETINAL COMPLEX: Normal thickness and contour bilaterally. Retinal layers are completely attached with no posterior vitreous detachment (PVD) or retinal tear/detachment.
- OPTIC NERVE HEADS & RETROBULBAR SPACES: Normal optic disc excavation and retrobulbar optic nerve shadow bilaterally. Extraocular muscles are symmetric.